  "description": "What if one pizza maker had to bake a whole day of Domino's pizzas? We did the math.\n\nSources:\n- Domino's 101: Fun Facts (Domino's media site, Nov 2026 edition): https://media.dominos.com/assets/files/dominos-101-fun-facts.pdf\n\nFrom the cited page: Domino's stores across the globe sell an average of 4 million pizzas a day; Domino's World's Fastest Pizza Maker can make three large pizzas in 31.22 seconds; Domino's operates more than 22,700 stores in over 90 markets (Q3 2026). Our math: 31.22 seconds / 3 = about 10.4 seconds a pizza; 4,000,000 pizzas x 10.4 seconds = about 41.6 million seconds = about 482 days non-stop (a made-up scenario; real cooking, ovens and breaks not included). Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #dominos #pizza #whatif #howtheymakemoney",
